database_help = Start with a disposable in-memory database, or open a named database in this app’s storage. Opening the same name again demonstrates persistence. Browser databases use OPFS. Maintenance operates on the currently open database.
database_name = Database name
open_memory = New in-memory database
open_durable = Open or reopen named database
integrity_check = Check database integrity
checkpoint = Checkpoint write-ahead log
vacuum = Reclaim unused space
records_help = Save creates a typed note or updates the existing ID through generated model bindings. Refresh reads the full typed query, including changes made in the SQL console.
note_id = Record ID
note_title = Title
note_done = Done
save_note = Save note
delete_note = Delete note
refresh = Refresh
record_count = Number of records
records_result = Typed records as JSON
sql_help = Run one query to display up to 500 rows, or execute a SQL script. Statements change the current database; use a disposable database to experiment. Raw writes refresh the typed model cache.
sql_input = SQL statement or script
sql_result = Query results as JSON
run_query = Run query
run_statements = Execute statements
exchange_help = Export the typed notes as JSON to copy or save elsewhere. Paste JSON below to import it. Import replaces all notes, so export first if you need to retain them. Other SQL tables are unaffected.
exchange_json = JSON document to import or export
export_json = Export notes as JSON
import_json = Replace notes from JSON
log_help = The latest 200 engine statements, including typed writes and queries. Refresh to read the current trace. Native and in-memory browser databases trace here; durable browser databases trace in the browser’s developer console. SQL traces can contain record values.
clear_log = Clear SQL log
